      "content": "# YJExplorer source build guide\n\nThis package contains source code only. It intentionally excludes executable files,\ncompiled assemblies, build caches, runtime settings, logs, and machine-specific data.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Windows 10 or Windows 11 (x64)\n- .NET 8 SDK\n- Optional: Visual Studio 2022 with the \".NET desktop development\" workload\n\nCheck the SDK installation:\n\n```powershell\ndotnet --info\n```\n\n## Build from a terminal\n\nOpen PowerShell in the extracted `YJExplorer-Source-*` folder and run:\n\n```powershell\ndotnet restore .\\FileManager.sln --configfile .\\NuGet.Config\ndotnet build .\\FileManager.sln -c Release\n```\n\nThe rebuilt program will be located at:\n\n```text\nFileManager\\bin\\x64\\Release\\net8.0-windows\\FileManager.exe\n```\n\nRun a Debug build while developing:\n\n```powershell\ndotnet build .\\FileManager.sln -c Debug\n```\n\n## Build with Visual Studio\n\n1. Open `FileManager.sln` in Visual Studio 2022.\n2. Select `Release` and `x64` in the toolbar.\n3. Choose **Build > Build Solution**.\n4. Start the `FileManager` project.\n\n## Project structure\n\n- `FileManager/App.xaml*`: application startup and single-instance handling\n- `FileManager/MainWindow.xaml*`: main menu, favorites bar, and Pane layouts\n- `FileManager/Controls/`: file Pane, settings, preview, rename, and dialog windows\n- `FileManager/Models/`: settings, Pane state, and file item models\n- `FileManager/Services/`: filesystem, file operations, Windows Shell menus/icons,\n  preview, settings persistence, and single-instance communication\n- `FileManager/Helpers/`: shortcut, formatting, converters, and visual-tree helpers\n\n## Runtime notes\n\n- This is a Windows-only WPF application and uses Windows Shell APIs.\n- No third-party NuGet package is currently required. `NuGet.Config` points only to\n  the public NuGet.org feed for normal SDK restore behavior.\n- `settings.json` is created beside the rebuilt executable when settings are saved.\n  It is not included in the source package because it can contain personal paths,\n  favorites, window positions, and preferences.\n- File previews depend on thumbnail and preview handlers installed on the home PC.\n  DWG preview availability therefore depends on installed CAD or preview software.\n- The contact address `yj@poscoenc.com` is intentionally present in two source files.\n  Change it before building if the home version should use a different address.\n\n## Source package safety\n\n`SOURCE_MANIFEST.txt` lists every packaged source file and its SHA-256 hash. The\npackage creation script rejects executables, DLLs, PDBs, logs, databases, archives,\nand files from `bin` or `obj` before creating the ZIP.\n"
    }
